      "id": "c2920539-352a-40b7-9f23-d680eb5d8281",
      "text": "I went to a bakery this morning, about a 10 minute walk away, that had local sweets that are only found in the Kathmandu valley. The Sel Roti you can find across Nepal, but another treat was a crispy Kakhamari (or Jalebi) with chaku (sugarcane wheat paste) wrapped in a flexible thin pita thing.",
      "type": "text"
